                <mxCell id="128" value="Not all fraud proofs are applicable to kill a dispute - only if the dispute has invalid strucutre in isolation will it be killed, otherwise it will persist and be part of reduce.&lt;div&gt;E.g. if a Double Sign is detected while syncing the stateProof of a dispute, that doesn&#39;t break the strucuture of a valid dispute, it just leaks information that leads the author to be slashed normaly without killing the dispute. If a InvalidState transition is detected, that does break the structure of a valid dispute and as such that is enough to kill the dispute on-chain.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="127" vertex="1">
